  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preservation of 3rd-Century BC Objects from the Greco-Roman City of Karanis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the preservation of 3rd-century BC objects from the Greco-Roman city of Karanis (present-day Kom Aushim) and establish and promote good conservation practices and public presentation of archaeological sites. The Pharonic-era objects from Karanis are stored under poor conditions, while political and economic circumstances in Egypt hamper the abilities of local conservators to care for them. The project involves a collections assessment, preventive conservation of the objects, and the development of a management plan for the site.</narrative>
  </description>
